# -- Scopes and Spaces -- #

# Scopes allow you to do stuff without worrying about the stack.
# at the end of a scope (declared through "{" and "}") the stack is reset.

1337 puts
{
	21 21 + puts
	{
		66 puts
	}
	puts
}
puts

# Spaces work similarly to scopes, but they will keep the top of the stack
# This is handy for loop conditions, ifs or side calculations

42
( 4 3 1 + + puts ) puts # this will print 8 8

42
{ 4 3 1 + + puts } puts # where as this will print 8 42

# both scopes and spaces are mostly syntactic sugar, but they allow you to write more concise (and readable code)
